WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.975
To close.

2
00:00:00.975 --> 00:00:03.711
The decisions are who owns each namespace,

3
00:00:03.711 --> 00:00:09.028
which middleware platform and so which
resolver path, the hub design in each cloud,

4
00:00:09.028 --> 00:00:12.389
and whether Oracle's private
access is needed at all,

5
00:00:12.389 --> 00:00:14.813
remembering that it's routing, not DNS.

6
00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:17.859
The next steps are the things
that couldn't be verified,

7
00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:21.515
such as which Oracle environment
the agency's tenant will use and

8
00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:25.374
Oracle's government-realm DNS limits;
they're all listed in the backup.

9
00:00:25.374 --> 00:00:31.282
In the workbook, the HR-Driven Identity
book and the DNS, DHCP and IPAM book cover

10
00:00:31.282 --> 00:00:37.012
those two halves in depth, and three
related research items sit beside this one.

11
00:00:37.012 --> 00:00:41.938
This is research under review, not an
endorsement by any federal agency.

12
00:00:41.938 --> 00:00:42.770
Thank you.
